9539	{"artifactId":"LLD-c32aa60534232f36-s2","entry":{"id":"review-c73e9ef661b5b68d726f62bb16a864b0","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:21:11.256Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's three design subsections (3.1-3.3) and test-acceptance mapping cover all three DEF acceptance criteria for s2 (ac1 row-universe enumeration, ac2 multi-row evidence linking with rejection of unsupported satisfaction, ac3 retention of deleted/unplanned/unavailable changes as explicit rows) and build nothing beyond the HLD-assigned sc2 scope (no reviewer-turn execution, no CR publication).","evidence":"DEF-c32aa60534232f36.json s2 acceptanceCriteria ac1/ac2/ac3 text matches almost verbatim what LLD §3.1-3.3 design and §6 acceptance-mapping table implement/test; HLD storyBoundaries.s2 ('do not execute reviewer turns or publish CRs') is respected — the LLD's postconditions explicitly state 'no storage, dispatch, approval or terminal verdict emitted'. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-c32aa60534232f36.json]","action":"Compared DEF-c32aa60534232f36.json s2 criteria against LLD §3 and §6.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's description of s1's existing, approved building blocks (ReviewSubjectV1/CommitPacketV1 shape, ReviewRuntimePortsV1, ReviewReadReceiptV1 with its 'reference/sourceDigest/contentRef/text/lines/completeness/limitations' fields, and the functions readApprovedWork/readReviewSource/snapshotValue/freezeValue/digestValue) matches the real, already-built code exactly.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/investigation/types.ts defines ReviewReadReceiptV1 and ReviewRuntimePortsV1 identically to the HLD sc6 sketch; src/workflow/code-review/investigation/work.ts:34 exports readApprovedWork, src/workflow/code-review/investigation/source.ts:55 exports readReviewSource, and identity.ts exports snapshotValue/freezeValue/digestValue exactly as cited in [[c1]]/[[c4]]/[[c5]]. [files: src/workflow/code-review/investigation/types.ts, src/workflow/code-review/investigation/work.ts, src/workflow/code-review/investigation/source.ts, src/workflow/code-review/investigation/identity.ts]","action":"Read investigation/types.ts, work.ts, source.ts, identity.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"'ledger-types.ts' and 'ledger.ts' with initializeReviewLedger/applyReviewLedgerDelta/validateReviewLedger are correctly labelled new (no such files/functions exist yet), and the reused primitives (snapshotValue/freezeValue/digestValue) genuinely exist with the stated signatures.","evidence":"No ledger.ts or ledger-types.ts exists under src/workflow/code-review/investigation/ (only types.ts, identity.ts, subject.ts, work.ts, source.ts, git-packets.ts, index.ts); identity.ts's snapshotValue<T>, freezeValue<T>, digestValue(unknown) match the reuse claim exactly. [files: src/workflow/code-review/investigation/identity.ts]","action":"Globbed src/workflow/code-review/investigation/*.ts and read identity.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"§3.1's plan to reuse 'adherenceObligations and ADHERENCE_LLD_SECTIONS/EXCLUDED' and 'narrow its accepted subject type ... preserving existing callers' is a complete, safe account of that function's real callers and contract.","evidence":"adherenceObligations(subject: CodeReviewSubject) lives in src/workflow/review-pipeline/adapters/code-review-obligations.ts and is called from src/workflow/review-pipeline/code-review.ts and src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/adherence.ts. adherence.ts itself reads subject.changedFiles and other CodeReviewSubject fields beyond approvedLld/approvedPlan (confirmed via grep: subject.approvedLld/approvedPlan/changedFiles at lines 81-162), and the same module backs the functional-coverage, coverage and conventions dimensions. The LLD never enumerates these real call sites or their field needs, only a hedged 'if needed' — the contract/change-site inventory for this reused surface is incomplete. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/adapters/code-review-obligations.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/adherence.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/code-review.ts]","action":"Grepped adherence.ts for subject.* field usage and located all callers of code-review-obligations.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Migration §7 correctly states zero downtime, no data rewrite and no persisted-schema change, because sc2 (EvidenceCoverageV1/ReviewLedgerV1) is a brand-new, not-yet-built value model with nothing stored on disk to migrate.","evidence":"No ledger.ts/ledger-types.ts or any ReviewLedgerV1 persistence exists yet (confirmed via glob of investigation/*.ts); HLD phase B (s2) explicitly states 'evidence/coverage state remains outside workflow artifact JSON' with no current CR schema change. [files: .insrc/artifacts/HLD-c32aa60534232f36.json]","action":"Globbed investigation/*.ts for any existing ledger persistence and cross-checked HLD phase B backwardCompat note.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"§3.1's plan to reuse-and-possibly-modify 'src/workflow/review-pipeline/adapters/code-review-obligations.ts' stays inside this epic's (c32aa60534232f36) HLD-sanctioned scope and does not contradict the LLD's own §3.3 claim of 'No changes to legacy coverage adapters, controller validation or CR schemas.'","evidence":"code-review-obligations.ts's own header attributes it to 'Epic 8315a11f s3' (the chunked-review-pipeline epic), and src/workflow/code-review/types.ts attributes CodeReviewSubject to a third, separate epic ('Code-review Epic E20260803/761a43a6fa645815'). Neither is listed among HLD-c32aa60534232f36's declared reuse seams ('src/workflow/code-review/subject.ts, grounding.ts, freshness.ts, gate.ts, src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts, repo-lifecycle.ts') or sharedContracts/storyBoundaries, so this epic's HLD never authorized touching it. §3.1 nonetheless proposes narrowing its parameter type, which is exactly the kind of legacy 'coverage adapter' §3.3 says is unchanged — a direct internal contradiction, and an out-of-epic boundary reach that an amendment to the owning epic would normally be required for. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/adapters/code-review-obligations.ts, src/workflow/code-review/types.ts, .insrc/artifacts/HLD-c32aa60534232f36.json]","action":"Read code-review-obligations.ts header/attribution and src/workflow/code-review/types.ts header, and cross-checked HLD architectureShape's declared reuse-seam list.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed ReviewLedgerError codes (invalid-input, subject-mismatch, provenance-mismatch, unknown-reference, conflicting-replay, unsupported-obligation, resource-limit) follow the same typed-error convention already established in this module family, so the design is buildable consistently with existing code.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/investigation/types.ts already defines SubjectPreparationError (codes invalid-input/unapproved-contract/stale-contract/invalid-object/ambiguous-attribution/unsupported-change/resource-limit) and ReviewRuntimePortError (invalid-value/invalid-identity/stale-generation/sequence-conflict/unknown-reference) as discriminated Error subclasses with a `code` field — the same pattern the LLD's ReviewLedgerError proposes to extend. [files: src/workflow/code-review/investigation/types.ts]","action":"Read investigation/types.ts error class definitions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of s2's three DEF acceptance criteria (ac1, ac2, ac3) maps to at least one named test in the LLD's §6 acceptance-mapping table, and those named tests appear among the unit/integration test subjects listed earlier in §6.","evidence":"§6 table: ac1→'review-s2-ac1 exact row universe'+LLD-section/integration test; ac2→'review-s2-ac2 ...'+pinned-receipt integration test; ac3→'review-s2-ac3 ...'+atomic-rejection/history test — each named test also appears verbatim in the unit/integration 'Subjects' lists just above the table, so the mapping is self-consistent (not dangling references).","action":"Cross-checked the acceptance-mapping table against the unit/integration Subjects lists in LLD §6.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":1,"low":6,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-28T13:21:11.256Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
